title: Settings › Pause › Pause all agents
route: /settings
intro: One red button stops all sixteen agents, after one question. The page then shows an amber banner and a green 'Resume all agents' button. In the demo, nothing outside this page changes.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the pause lives in the page and is lost when the person leaves Settings. The real rules for a pause (PRD FR-25) are shown in orange.
---
screen s1 "Settings\nHeader button 'Pause all agents', red outline, with a pause icon"
click c1 "Click 'Pause all agents'"
overlay o1 "Pause all agents?\n'No checks, calls or drafts will run until you resume.'"
process p1 "'Requests already with a payer stay where they are. You can resume at any time.'"
decision q1 "Which button?"
click k1 "Click 'Cancel', click the X, press Escape, or click the dimmed area"
endx x1 "Pop-up closes\nNothing changes and no toast"
click k2 "Click 'Pause all'\nRed outline button"

group gDo "What 'Pause all' does"
  store a1 "All sixteen agent switches go off\nEven the ones already off"
  process a2 "Pop-up closes"
  toast a3 "'All agents paused'\nAmber toast"
  toast a4 "Banner under the header, amber\n'All agents are paused'\n'Nothing is being checked, drafted or sent until you resume them. In this demo the pause does not change the other screens.'"
  process a5 "Header button becomes 'Resume all agents'\nGreen, filled, with a play-pause icon"
endgroup

process n1 "Freedom levels are not touched\nEach agent keeps the level it had"

group gReal "Production (PRD FR-25)"
  process r1 "Production: a pause takes effect before the next step of any running job"
  process r2 "Production: outbound steps already running finish, or roll back to the manual queue\nNever half-submitted"
endgroup

click k3 "Click 'Resume all agents'"
store b1 "All sixteen switches go back on"
toast b2 "'Agents resumed'\nGreen toast. The banner goes and the red button returns"
end e1 "Page is back to normal\nFreedom levels are as they were"
goto g1 "Continues in: Settings › Pause › What the rest of the app shows"
goto g2 "Continues in: Settings › Pause › Pause one agent, resume all"

s1 --> c1 --> o1 --> p1 --> q1
q1 -->|Leave| k1 --> x1
q1 -->|Pause all| k2 --> a1 & a3
a1 --> a2 --> a4 --> a5
a5 --> n1
a5 --> k3 --> b1 & b2
b1 --> e1
b2 --> e1
a5 -.-> r1
r1 --> r2
a4 -.-> g1
a5 -.-> g2
